// `[a, b, box] := f()` is not Pine. TV reports exactly ONE error, at the `:=`:
//
//     Mismatched input ":=" expecting set "="
//
// We report the same defect at the same position with our own wording (see
// TODO #79 for that), and used to add one `"<name>" is already defined` per
// name on top - the invalid form was still re-declaring names the earlier `=`
// had introduced. TradingView emits none of those.
//
//     pine-lint -H <this file>   -> exactly 1 error, at the `:=`
//
// This lives in a probe rather than a regression fixture because the cascade
// is a VALIDATION effect behind a PARSE error, and the fixture harness skips
// validation once parsing fails - an `errors: N` directive there is vacuous
// and cannot go red. Verified by mutation: suppressing the fix leaves the
// fixture green. See AGENTS.md on that harness limitation.
//@version=6
indicator("tuple reassignment")
[a, b, box] = ta.macd(close, 12, 26, 9)
[a, b, box] := ta.macd(close, 12, 26, 9)
plot(a + b + box)
